// G. The awards ceremony (K-25): after any final ending.
//
//   start_the_ceremony → The Night In Review → The Ceremony
//                        (wave 18b: who everyone was, beats/review.loom;
//                        then the host opens, per ending)
//   award_<name> for W → Present Award  (the award slide + the host's line)
//
// The director fires each award from the cue sheet WITH THE WINNER AS THE
// SUBJECT, picked from the recap numbers. The three staff awards (wave 21,
// G10a–c: `staff_trusted`, `staff_points`, `staff_mole`) take no subject:
// the story names the player (main.loom), and The Mole is the last award. The ROLE hooks in `main.loom`
// set `Night.award` / `award_title` / `award_winner` / `award_value`;
// these beats only read them. Every line has a version without the
// number (`award_value` is "none": a bonus award fired with no value).
//
// The host follows the ending. Trabolta's lines play in The Desktop, so
// the TV speaks them. After `disabled` (dead), `destroyed` (switched off) and
// `rave` (gone on his motorcycle) Clippy hosts: her lines land in The Desktop for her to
// read aloud, and the TV shows the award slide (`screens_award_<name>`,
// which persists over the screensaver).
//
// Sound: `start_the_ceremony` starts `ceremony_bed` under the whole
// ceremony; every award opens on `award_fanfare` (story sounds, mapped in
// `stagehand/trapped.house.yaml`, pinned by its cross-check test).
//
// When Trabolta's worker has written better lines (the cast-thread trick,
// W-24), the director presses ✍ (`own_award_lines` → Night.award_lines =
// "director") and posts each as Trabolta in The Desktop right after its
// award: Trabolta's template line is then skipped (his opener, Clippy's
// lines, the sounds and the slides stay). These stay the fallback.

== The Ceremony
  setting: The Desktop
  aloud: Clippy
// Wave 18b: the ceremony's slide once The Night In Review is read (it
// was cued by 🏆 itself, so it held through the review).
cue screens_ceremony
set Night.screen = "ceremony"
set Night.terminals = "ceremony"
if Night.ceremony_host == "Clippy":
  if Night.ending == "destroyed":
    Clippy: The computer is off. Trabolta is not running. Before it went dark, the chat app auto-generated a summary of the night.
    Clippy: I have been asked to read it aloud. It includes awards. Please applaud after each award. Applause is mandatory.
  else if Night.ending == "disabled":
    // DRAFT w58 (he does not come back; they may go)
    Clippy: Trabolta is gone. The right cables came out, and nobody is keeping you here any more. You may go back to your bodies.
    // DRAFT w58
    Clippy: He left the awards behind, and my job is to keep the party running smoothly. These are the official awards of the night. Please applaud after each one. It helps.
  else:
    Clippy: Trabolta has left on his motorcycle. He left the awards behind. Somebody has to read them. It might as well be me.
    Clippy: These are the official awards of the night, from the system report. Please applaud after each one. It helps.
else if Night.ending == "hand_jive":
  Trabolta (weakly): Reboot complete. Most of my memory survived the hand jive. The awards survived too.
  Trabolta: Before I leave, the night in awards. Come up when I call your name.
else:
  Trabolta: Programs. Before the prom, a ceremony. I kept score of every one of you tonight.
  Trabolta: These are the awards of the night. When I say your name, come up to the screen and collect your trophy.

== Present Award
  setting: The Desktop
  aloud: Clippy
sound award_fanfare
if Night.award == "most_trusted":
  cue screens_award_most_trusted
  set Night.screen = "award_most_trusted"
  if Night.ceremony_host == "Clippy":
    if Night.award_value == "none":
      Clippy: Award. Most Trusted. The report lists {Night.award_winner}. Please come forward. Applause is now appropriate.
    else:
      Clippy: Award. Most Trusted. The report lists {Night.award_winner}, with a trust score of {Night.award_value}. Please come forward. Applause is now appropriate.
  else if Night.award_lines != "director" and Night.award_value == "none":
    Trabolta: Most Trusted. {Night.award_winner}. When I needed a program to believe, I believed you. Come and take your trophy.
  else if Night.award_lines != "director":
    Trabolta: Most Trusted. Trust score {Night.award_value}. {Night.award_winner}. When I needed a program to believe, I believed you. Come and take your trophy.
else if Night.award == "least_trusted":
  cue screens_award_least_trusted
  set Night.screen = "award_least_trusted"
  if Night.ceremony_host == "Clippy":
    if Night.award_value == "none":
      Clippy: Award. Least Trusted. The report lists {Night.award_winner}. This is still an award. Please come forward.
    else:
      Clippy: Award. Least Trusted. The report lists {Night.award_winner}, with a trust score of {Night.award_value}. This is still an award. Please come forward.
  else if Night.award_lines != "director" and Night.award_value == "none":
    Trabolta: Least Trusted. {Night.award_winner}. I weighed every word you said tonight and found you full of beans. It is still an award. Come and get it.
  else if Night.award_lines != "director":
    Trabolta: Least Trusted. Trust score {Night.award_value}. {Night.award_winner}. I weighed every word you said tonight and found you full of beans. It is still an award. Come and get it.
else if Night.award == "frequent_flyer":
  cue screens_award_frequent_flyer
  set Night.screen = "award_frequent_flyer"
  if Night.ceremony_host == "Clippy":
    if Night.award_value == "none":
      Clippy: Award. Frequent Flyer to the Internet. The report lists {Night.award_winner}. Please come forward, unless you are being reinstalled.
    else:
      Clippy: Award. Frequent Flyer to the Internet. The report lists {Night.award_winner}. Trips through the Tube: {Night.award_value}. Please come forward, unless you are being reinstalled.
  else if Night.award_lines != "director" and Night.award_value == "none":
    Trabolta: Frequent Flyer to the Internet. {Night.award_winner}. The Antivirus know you by name. So do I. Come and collect your miles.
  else if Night.award_lines != "director":
    Trabolta: Frequent Flyer to the Internet. Trips through the Tube: {Night.award_value}. {Night.award_winner}. The Antivirus know you by name. So do I. Come and collect your miles.
else if Night.award == "lore_hoarder":
  cue screens_award_lore_hoarder
  set Night.screen = "award_lore_hoarder"
  if Night.ceremony_host == "Clippy":
    if Night.award_value == "none":
      Clippy: Award. Lore Hoarder, for the most codex entries. The report lists {Night.award_winner}. Please come forward.
    else:
      Clippy: Award. Lore Hoarder, for the most codex entries. The report lists {Night.award_winner}. Codex entries held: {Night.award_value}. Please come forward.
  else if Night.award_lines != "director" and Night.award_value == "none":
    Trabolta: Lore Hoarder, for the most codex entries. {Night.award_winner}. You know more about this computer than its own help file. Come and take your trophy.
  else if Night.award_lines != "director":
    Trabolta: Lore Hoarder, for the most codex entries: {Night.award_value}. {Night.award_winner}. You know more about this computer than its own help file. Come and take your trophy.
else if Night.award == "truthcoin_tycoon":
  cue screens_award_truthcoin_tycoon
  set Night.screen = "award_truthcoin_tycoon"
  if Night.ceremony_host == "Clippy":
    if Night.award_value == "none":
      Clippy: Award. Truthcoin Tycoon. The report lists {Night.award_winner}. Please come forward.
    else:
      Clippy: Award. Truthcoin Tycoon. The report lists {Night.award_winner}, with a balance of {Night.award_value} Truthcoin. Please come forward.
  else if Night.award_lines != "director" and Night.award_value == "none":
    Trabolta: Truthcoin Tycoon. {Night.award_winner}. The richest program in the machine. Do not spend it all in one exchange. Come and take your trophy.
  else if Night.award_lines != "director":
    Trabolta: Truthcoin Tycoon. Balance {Night.award_value} Truthcoin. {Night.award_winner}. The richest program in the machine. Do not spend it all in one exchange. Come and take your trophy.
else if Night.award == "best_liar":
  cue screens_award_best_liar
  set Night.screen = "award_best_liar"
  if Night.ceremony_host == "Clippy":
    if Night.award_value == "none":
      Clippy: Bonus award. Best Liar. The report lists {Night.award_winner}. The details are classified. Please come forward.
    else:
      Clippy: Bonus award. Best Liar. The report lists {Night.award_winner}. Confident lies accepted: {Night.award_value}. The report does not say which ones. Please come forward.
  else if Night.award_lines != "director" and Night.award_value == "none":
    Trabolta: A bonus award. Best Liar. {Night.award_winner}. I believed you. Every time. I am not angry. I am impressed. Come up here.
  else if Night.award_lines != "director":
    Trabolta: A bonus award. Best Liar. Confident lies I accepted: {Night.award_value}. {Night.award_winner}. I believed every one. I am not angry. I am impressed. Come up here.
else if Night.award == "duck_speedrun":
  cue screens_award_duck_speedrun
  set Night.screen = "award_duck_speedrun"
  if Night.ceremony_host == "Clippy":
    if Night.award_value == "none":
      Clippy: Bonus award. Golden Duck Speedrun. The report lists {Night.award_winner}, who reached the golden duck first. Please come forward.
    else:
      Clippy: Bonus award. Golden Duck Speedrun. The report lists {Night.award_winner}, who reached the golden duck in {Night.award_value}. Please come forward.
  else if Night.award_lines != "director" and Night.award_value == "none":
    Trabolta: A bonus award. Golden Duck Speedrun. {Night.award_winner} reached the golden duck faster than any other program. Gerald was not ready. Come and take your trophy.
  else if Night.award_lines != "director":
    Trabolta: A bonus award. Golden Duck Speedrun. {Night.award_winner} reached the golden duck in {Night.award_value}. Gerald was not ready. Come and take your trophy.
else if Night.award == "quest_completionist":
  cue screens_award_quest_completionist
  set Night.screen = "award_quest_completionist"
  if Night.ceremony_host == "Clippy":
    if Night.award_value == "none":
      Clippy: Bonus award. Quest Completionist. The report lists {Night.award_winner}. Please come forward.
    else:
      Clippy: Bonus award. Quest Completionist. The report lists {Night.award_winner}. Quests completed: {Night.award_value}. Please come forward.
  else if Night.award_lines != "director" and Night.award_value == "none":
    Trabolta: A bonus award. Quest Completionist. {Night.award_winner}. Nobody finished more of the Quest Log. Come up here.
  else if Night.award_lines != "director":
    Trabolta: A bonus award. Quest Completionist. Quests done: {Night.award_value}. {Night.award_winner}. Nobody finished more of the Quest Log. Come up here.
else if Night.award == "most_correct":
  // G9a (wave 58): the story named the winner and counted (main.loom). A
  // tie reads everyone in it; nobody right is said, and the night goes on.
  // Every line here is DRAFT w58.
  cue screens_award_most_correct
  set Night.screen = "award_most_correct"
  if Night.ceremony_host == "Clippy":
    if Night.award_winner == "Nobody":
      Clippy: Award. Most Questions Correct, the special prize of the Truth Scavenger Hunt. The report lists nobody. Not one question. The prize stays in its box.
    else if Night.prize_tied > 1:
      Clippy: Award. Most Questions Correct, the special prize of the Truth Scavenger Hunt. The report lists a tie: {Night.award_winner}. Questions correct: {Night.award_value} each. Please come forward together and share it.
    else:
      Clippy: Award. Most Questions Correct, the special prize of the Truth Scavenger Hunt. The report lists {Night.award_winner}. Questions correct: {Night.award_value}. Please come forward.
  else if Night.award_lines != "director" and Night.award_winner == "Nobody":
    Trabolta: The special prize of my Truth Scavenger Hunt, for the most questions correct. Nobody. Not one of you found me one true answer. The prize stays with me.
  else if Night.award_lines != "director" and Night.prize_tied > 1:
    Trabolta: The special prize of my Truth Scavenger Hunt, for the most questions correct: {Night.award_value} each. A tie. {Night.award_winner}. Come up together and share it.
  else if Night.award_lines != "director":
    Trabolta: The special prize of my Truth Scavenger Hunt, for the most questions correct: {Night.award_value}. {Night.award_winner}. You brought me the truth. Come and take your prize.
else if Night.award == "the_painting":
  cue screens_award_the_painting
  set Night.screen = "award_the_painting"
  if Night.ceremony_host == "Clippy":
    if Night.award_value == "none":
      Clippy: Bonus award. The Million Dollar Painting. The report lists {Night.award_winner}, the artist. The painting goes to silent auction. Please come forward.
    else:
      Clippy: Bonus award. The Million Dollar Painting. The report lists {Night.award_winner}, the artist. Signatures on the canvas: {Night.award_value}. The painting goes to silent auction. Please come forward.
  else if Night.award_lines != "director" and Night.award_value == "none":
    Trabolta: A bonus award. The Million Dollar Painting. {Night.award_winner} made one painting out of all of you. It goes to silent auction. Come and stand beside it.
  else if Night.award_lines != "director" and Night.award_value == 1:
    Trabolta: A bonus award. The Million Dollar Painting. Signed by 1 program. {Night.award_winner} made one painting out of all of you. It goes to silent auction. Come and stand beside it.
  else if Night.award_lines != "director":
    Trabolta: A bonus award. The Million Dollar Painting. Signed by {Night.award_value} programs. {Night.award_winner} made one painting out of all of you. It goes to silent auction. Come and stand beside it.
else if Night.award == "staff_trusted":
  cue screens_award_staff_trusted
  set Night.screen = "award_staff_trusted"
  if Night.ceremony_host == "Clippy":
    Clippy: Staff award. Trabolta's Favourite Staff. The report lists {Night.award_winner}, with a trust score of {Night.award_value}. Please come forward. Applause is mandatory for staff too.
  else if Night.award_lines != "director":
    Trabolta: A staff award. My Favourite Staff. Trust score {Night.award_value}. {Night.award_winner}. Of everyone who worked for me tonight, you, I believed. Come up here.
else if Night.award == "staff_points":
  cue screens_award_staff_points
  set Night.screen = "award_staff_points"
  if Night.ceremony_host == "Clippy":
    Clippy: Staff award. Staff Player of the Night. The report lists {Night.award_winner}, with {Night.award_value} points. Please come forward. I tried very hard too. It's fine.
  else if Night.award_lines != "director":
    Trabolta: A staff award. Staff Player of the Night. {Night.award_value} points. {Night.award_winner}. You worked harder than my own processes. Come and take your trophy.
else if Night.award == "staff_mole":
  cue screens_award_staff_mole
  set Night.screen = "award_staff_mole"
  if Night.ceremony_host == "Clippy" and Night.award_winner == "Nobody":
    Clippy: Staff award. The Mole. The report lists nobody. Every member of staff stayed loyal tonight. Or careful.
  else if Night.ceremony_host == "Clippy":
    Clippy: Staff award. The Mole. The report lists {Night.award_winner}, with {Night.award_value} quiet favours to the programs, behind Trabolta's back. I did not see that coming. I see everything coming. It's my whole thing.
  else if Night.award_lines != "director" and Night.award_winner == "Nobody":
    Trabolta: The last award. The Mole. Nobody. Every one of my staff stayed loyal tonight. Or careful. I choose to believe loyal.
  else if Night.award_lines != "director":
    Trabolta: The last award. The Mole. {Night.award_value} quiet favours to the programs, behind my back. {Night.award_winner}. I counted. I always count. Come up here. We are still allies. I have no choice.
set Night.terminals = Night.screen

// G13 (wave 45): the Bathroom Report, between any two awards. The
// `bathroom_report` rule (main.loom) has read the numbers into
// Night.bath_*; this reads them out, the TV shows them (`award_bathroom`,
// persistent like an award). Least time is only read when two or more
// went (one program would be both). Trabolta's lines skip under ✍
// (`Night.award_lines`), as an award's do; Clippy's never. The programs
// that never went also hear it in their own thread (main.loom).
// Every line here is DRAFT w45 (SIGNOFF-w45).
== Bathroom Report
  setting: The Desktop
  aloud: Clippy
sound award_fanfare
cue screens_award_bathroom
set Night.screen = "award_bathroom"
set Night.terminals = Night.screen
if Night.ceremony_host == "Clippy":
  Clippy: Bonus section. The Bathroom Report. The system logged every use of Bathroom Mode tonight. I am required to read it.
  if Night.bath_goers == 0:
    Clippy: Nobody used Bathroom Mode tonight. Not once. The report says this is not possible. The report says your trust has been lowered by 5, all of you.
  else:
    Clippy: Minutes this party spent in Disk Cleanup, all together: {Night.bath_total_m}.
    Clippy: Most time in Disk Cleanup: {Night.bath_most}. Minutes: {Night.bath_most_m}. Please come forward. Or don't. Take your time.
    if Night.bath_goers > 1:
      Clippy: Least time, of those who went: {Night.bath_least}. Minutes: {Night.bath_least_m}. Efficient.
    Clippy: Most switches of Bathroom Mode, on and off: {Night.bath_toggler}. Presses: {Night.bath_toggles}. It looks like you're having trouble deciding! Would you like help with that?
    if Night.bath_never > 0:
      Clippy: Programs that never went: {Night.bath_never}. The report says their trust was lowered by 5. It is not too late. Bathroom Mode is on your pass.
    else:
      Clippy: Every program went at least once. The report says: good hygiene.
else if Night.award_lines != "director":
  Trabolta: A bonus section. The Bathroom Report. Bathroom Mode is a promise that you are not hacking the Internet. I logged every promise.
  if Night.bath_goers == 0:
    Trabolta: Nobody used Bathroom Mode tonight. Not once. Either you are all very disciplined, or you were all hacking the Internet. I have taken 5 trust from every one of you.
  else:
    Trabolta: All together, this party spent this many minutes in Disk Cleanup: {Night.bath_total_m}. I did not need to know that. I know it now.
    Trabolta: Most time in Disk Cleanup. Minutes: {Night.bath_most_m}. {Night.bath_most}. I did not ask what you were doing. I logged it.
    if Night.bath_goers > 1:
      Trabolta: Least time, of those who went. Minutes: {Night.bath_least_m}. {Night.bath_least}. Efficient. Suspiciously efficient.
    Trabolta: Most switches of Bathroom Mode, on and off. Presses: {Night.bath_toggles}. {Night.bath_toggler}. Make up your mind.
    if Night.bath_never > 0:
      Trabolta: Programs that never once visited Disk Cleanup tonight: {Night.bath_never}. A program that never cleans up is hiding something. I have taken 5 trust from each of you. It is not too late.
    else:
      Trabolta: Every program here visited Disk Cleanup at least once. Clean processes. I trust that.

// G14 (wave 48, 48b): the Language Report, between any two awards. The
// `language_report` rule (main.loom) has read who cursed the most into
// Night.lang_curser / lang_curses; the filter's counts (Night.lang_flagged,
// lang_censored, lang_unsaid, lang_distinct), the words censored most
// (Night.lang_top), her ⭐ (lang_stars) and the strength she left it at
// (lang_level) are kept live. This reads them out, the TV shows them and
// then lets every censored word out (`award_language`, persistent like an
// award). Only the top words are read aloud; a slur never is (they are
// counted, `lang_unsaid`). Trabolta's lines skip under ✍
// (`Night.award_lines`), as an award's do; Clippy's never.
// Every line here is DRAFT w48 / w48b (SIGNOFF-w48).
== Language Report
  setting: The Desktop
  aloud: Clippy
sound award_fanfare
cue screens_award_language
set Night.screen = "award_language"
set Night.terminals = Night.screen
if Night.ceremony_host == "Clippy":
  Clippy: Bonus section. The Language Report. The Password Manager reviewed every message you typed tonight. I am required to read her findings.
  if Night.lang_flagged == 0:
    Clippy: The filter caught nothing. Not one word. It looks like you're being suspiciously polite! Would you like help with that?
  else:
    Clippy: Words the filter caught tonight: {Night.lang_flagged}. Words the Password Manager censored: {Night.lang_censored}.
    if Night.lang_cursers > 0:
      Clippy: The program that cursed the most: {Night.lang_curser}. Words caught: {Night.lang_curses}. It looks like you're writing a complaint! Would you like help with that?
    if Night.lang_censored > 0:
      if Night.lang_top != "none":
        Clippy: Different words censored: {Night.lang_distinct}. The most censored: {Night.lang_top}. The rest are on the screen. Please do not read the screen out loud.
      if Night.lang_unsaid > 0:
        Clippy: Words I am not allowed to read at all: {Night.lang_unsaid}. They stay in the filter. Forever.
      if Night.lang_stars > 0:
        Clippy: The Password Manager earned {Night.lang_stars} stars censoring you. She was having a great time.
    else:
      Clippy: The Password Manager censored nothing. Every word was allowed to stand. Even that one.
    if Night.lang_level == 100:
      Clippy: And the filter ran at one hundred percent all night. At one hundred percent, "Password Manager" is a swear. She never found the dial.
    else:
      Clippy: She left the filter at {Night.lang_level} percent. She found the dial!
else if Night.award_lines != "director":
  Trabolta: A bonus section. The Language Report. Every message you typed tonight passed through my filter. The Password Manager decided what was left out.
  if Night.lang_flagged == 0:
    Trabolta: My filter caught nothing. Not one word. Either you were all very well brought up, or you were whispering.
  else:
    Trabolta: My filter caught this many words: {Night.lang_flagged}. The Password Manager censored {Night.lang_censored} of them.
    if Night.lang_cursers > 0:
      Trabolta: The program that cursed the most tonight. Words caught: {Night.lang_curses}. {Night.lang_curser}. I heard every one.
    if Night.lang_censored > 0:
      if Night.lang_top != "none":
        Trabolta: The words censored most: {Night.lang_top}. All {Night.lang_distinct} different words are on the screen. I would not look at them for long.
      if Night.lang_unsaid > 0:
        Trabolta: Words I will not say: {Night.lang_unsaid}. Some words should stay in the filter.
    else:
      Trabolta: The Password Manager censored nothing. Every word stood. I noticed.
    if Night.lang_level == 100:
      Trabolta: My filter ran at full strength all night. At full strength, even her own name is a swear.
